```ts
import type { GeospatialCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { setGeospatialOrientation } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function tiltGlobeCamera(camera: GeospatialCamera, pitch: number): void {
    camera.limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale = null;
    camera.center = camera.center;
    setGeospatialOrientation(camera, { pitch });
}
```

This:
1. Disables the radius-based pitch clamping, so the pitch stays at the target value regardless of zoom level.
2. Forces the limits change to take effect immediately via a center self-assignment.
3. Sets the pitch to the target value using the proper orientation API, which preserves yaw, radius, and center.

The camera will look at its center point at the specified tilt, and the tilt will persist through zoom changes because the radius-based clamping is disabled.
